From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lewis Gibson <12851394+lewisgibson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:04:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Answer an rcon command after the tasks it queued have run

Many commands that Folia dispatches to a region or to the global region (time,
xp query, enchant, place, weather, setblock, fill, forceload, worldborder and
more) send their feedback from the task they queue, after the command itself
has returned. The rcon connection was answered as soon as the command returned,
so the reply was empty, or missing the part that the task wrote. Only save-all
registered a completion to wait for.

The invariant: the rcon response of a command contains everything that the
tasks the command itself queued on RegionizedServer or on the tick task queues
wrote to the source, or the response is sent after at most 20 seconds. Only the
tasks queued by the thread that runs the command are waited for, not the tasks
those tasks queue in turn, so a plugin task that reschedules itself cannot hold
a response. Nothing else changes: the wait happens on the rcon thread, never on
a tick thread, and a task queued outside an rcon command is not wrapped.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
index aa575f3b76ef70ffb9f0410e7e5cfe7af384bfbd..54b6cec7941034b59c5b520f6cbc6e48dcacffcb 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedServer.java
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ public final class RegionizedServer {
     }
 
     public void addTask(final Runnable run) {
-        this.addTaskWithoutNotify(run);
+        this.addTaskWithoutNotify(net.minecraft.server.rcon.RconConsoleSource.trackQueuedTask(run)); // an rcon command is answered after the tasks it queued have run
         this.notifyTasks();
     }
 
